cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Community Goal — a town's first data center: what to require before saying yes"
message: >-
  If you use this guide, its requirements, or its API in a staff report, filing,
  or publication, please cite it. Requirement ids are permanent, so citing one
  (for example s9-r2) will mean the same thing next year.
type: dataset
abstract: >-
  A structured, open requirements guide for local governments facing a first data
  center proposal: ten sections and seventy-one requirements covering independent
  review, site suitability, instrument selection, water, noise, on-site
  generation, ratepayer and budget exposure, public return, financial security,
  and phased approval with funded closure. Published as an interactive site and a
  static JSON API, with community-contributed jurisdiction overlays.
authors:
  - name: "Community Goal contributors"
repository-code: "https://github.com/caffeinated1/configurationRotBot"
url: "https://caffeinated1.github.io/configurationRotBot/"
license: CC-BY-4.0
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2026-09-08"
keywords:
  - data centers
  - land use
  - local government
  - zoning
  - civic technology
  - open data
  - public participation
